🚽 Test case: #193 -- a function can return a pointer to a struct (`gang
🚽 Point *f()`), the last of #193's gaps. Returns a pointer PARAMETER (the
🚽 safe use: the pointee outlives the call, unlike returning `&local`).
🚽 Reads and writes through the returned pointer alias the caller's struct
🚽 (composing with #196). The discarded `pick(&p, &q);` statement checks
🚽 that releasing the return slot does NOT free the borrowed pointee (a
🚽 pointer-to-struct return's value is not an owned blob).
gang Point {
    rizz x;
    rizz y;
};

gang Point *pick(gang Point *a, gang Point *b) {
    bussin a;
}

skibidi main {
    gang Point p;
    p.x = 1;
    p.y = 2;
    gang Point q;
    q.x = 3;
    q.y = 4;
    gang Point *r = pick(&p, &q);
    yapping("%d %d", r.x, r.y);
    r.x = 99;
    yapping("%d", p.x);
    pick(&p, &q);
    yapping("%d %d", p.x, q.x);
}
